A WITHOUT ROWID table, rebuilt: its key's own index (SQLite's, unnamed by
schema.sql) goes and comes with it.

== before
CREATE TABLE tag (dish_id INTEGER NOT NULL, label TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (dish_id, label)) STRICT, WITHOUT ROWID;
INSERT INTO tag VALUES (1, 'hot'), (1, 'vegan');

== after
CREATE TABLE tag (dish_id INTEGER NOT NULL, label TEXT NOT NULL, weight INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1, PRIMARY KEY (dish_id, label)) STRICT, WITHOUT ROWID;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `tag`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "tag" RENAME TO "roux_old_tag"
  table `tag`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE tag (dish_id INTEGER NOT NULL, label TEXT NOT NULL, weight INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1, PRIMARY KEY (dish_id, label)) STRICT, WITHOUT ROWID
  table `tag`: its rows, by dish_id, label
    INSERT INTO "tag" ("dish_id", "label") SELECT "dish_id", "label" FROM "roux_old_tag"
  table `tag`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_tag"
